config FEATHER_NRF9151_DEBUG_ACCESS_OPEN
	bool "Keep debug access open across resets"
	depends on PARTITION_MANAGER
	default y
	help
	  Merge uicr_debug_access_open.hex into merged.hex. It writes the
	  HwUnprotected value (0x50FA50FA) to UICR.APPROTECT and
	  UICR.SECUREAPPROTECT, so images built with
	  CONFIG_NRF_(SECURE_)APPROTECT_USE_UICR reopen the debug port on every
	  boot. Without it, the nRF91x1 locks the debug port after each pin or
	  power-on reset until the chip is erased.

	  The UICR words can only be written from the erased state, so this takes
	  effect on a full erase and flash. Disable for production.

	  Only merged.hex carries the words. The images' own hex files, and the
	  update images built from them, never touch UICR.
